    "turn_text": "affordable housing. So several bills we worked on passed into law include helping folks get TPS who are Venezuelan descent during the issues, you know, we have a huge amount of folks coming in who, down there, it's a communist, murderous dictatorship. It's very sad. We helped out with working to make the Kissimmee River a while in Scenic River. This is a key area for conservation for hunting and recreation for wildlife that spans both Polk and Osceola County and cleans the water going into Lake Okeechobian out to the Everglades. So we just got a study and to push that along to make it a wild and scenic river. Senator Rubio and I passed the Restoring Resilient Reefs Act which reauthorizes funding to restore our reefs. The Great Florida Reef is the third largest reef track in the world and it's having challenges because of pollution, because of warming seas. And so we're working with local folks like SeaWorld and others to help rebuild the reef. We're helping with improving infrastructure to prevent pollution from going out and hurting the reef. And then, of course, we're working on climate issues and other major bills as well. So those were a couple bills just from this last term that we worked on that were a big help. Then a lot of the major things we're doing are just implementing major laws that pass. So last time we passed the investment job and infrastructure law, which was, excuse me, the investment infrastructure and jobs act, which Florida's getting upwards of about $50 billion over the next 10 years to help upgrade our roads to help with improving our clean water with the grid getting internet to all Americans. Our rural areas are falling behind with internet, so we're now finally getting that money down to do that. So everything from I4, which I'm sure those of you here in Southeastern know that to helping out with, we're going to see a potential Sun Rail expansion and Bright Line as well as a bunch of money coming down through the state r