    "turn_text": "but we usually get our water from the Florida, and so we're going to have to build some new reservoirs around here. It's affected jobs because we've had some major companies who were We're trying to get in, but they need enough water to do what they're doing. So just some issues that are directly affecting here in in Polk County. And then of course the the rural areas. We were just in Keenan'sville, Florida, which is in southern Polk County and our southern Osceola County and with our ranchers and folks who are who are managing hunting leases and some of these other opportunities down there. And it's amazing how much technology they need to download to track the quail or the awesome turkey or to have GPS for the cows. This is not your grandfather's agriculture. And so all these things are helping out with that. And then jobs. We are really focusing on a lot of the tech clusters throughout the area from Cape Canaveral, where we have the busiest spaceport in the world and we're Heading back to the moon, everybody. That's exciting. We are really excited about that. We do simulation training to help train our military at UCF. We have a medical city at Lake Nona, where we have Nemours in the VA hospital and others, and then in Neo-City, we're making microchips. So help them try to protect our environment, improve our infrastructure, and also bringing more higher-paying jobs to the region. So a lot of stuff we're working on, and it's all about improving the quality of life of our constituents.",
