    "turn_text": "there's jobs for us too. But of all these tech clusters that are coming in, STEM is really going to drive a lot of it. And look, math is hard, science is hard. So I'm saying that to tell people if you're looking to really provide for the future and you want to live here in Central Florida and you're looking for innovative new jobs. Of course, as we produce more and more in Central Florida, then that helps out everyone else from the local grocery store to the local law office to the barbershop to you name it restaurants because people who have money in their pockets support small businesses. So there'll be plenty of jobs for everybody. But the main ones are in aerospace and space. They're in simulation training and virtual reality as we train our troops to go into helicopters and tanks and all these different things. And they're in medical technology and advancing helping cure cancer and infectious diseases. They're in microchips, which we learned during the pandemic. We can't have all the microchips be built 10,000 miles away. Things can happen. The pandemic happened. The Ukraine war is happening. The",
