    "turn_idx": 75,
    "turn_text": "As opposed to someone who started out as like You know, the head of the HOA or the head of a local civic organization. They work with folks. They serve on boards. So by the time they run, they actually know what the job entails. And so that would be a big part of it. Working on some campaigns is helpful too. So you see that candidate debate, how to raise money, walk with, talk to constituents, knock on doors. So all those things working your way up and you don't have to take forever. I mean, an election cycle or two will help you with that. So those are helpful. And then knowledge is key. I'm constantly reading the paper. We're talking about Silicon Valley Bank before in our discussion and about the briefing that was very late at night. I had already read up for a day or two and was fully briefed on it by the time that came up. So there wasn't much I wasn't aware of. So knowledge is foundational. And then remember your community, right? All those folks you talked to, You need to remember all that you promise folks, all that you talked about what their aspirations are and you go in and you bring the dance partners who brought you there. Right. And you stand up for them. All those things are helpful.",
